## What this licence can and cannot grant

AV Atlas does not own the underlying bibliographic facts. This release is a
derived compilation — titles, author names, venues, years, categories
assigned by this project, and citation relationships computed by this project
— built from metadata published by:

CVF (Computer Vision Foundation) · DBLP · OpenAlex · arXiv ·
Semantic Scholar · ecva.net · the NeurIPS proceedings · PMLR ·
community-maintained venue listings

The CC BY-NC grant above applies to this project's own compilation and to the
values it computed. It does not, and cannot, override:

- **those sources' own terms of use**, which continue to apply to material
  obtained from them;
- **the rights of the papers' authors and publishers** in the papers
  themselves. This release contains bibliographic metadata only. It contains
  no full text and no figures. Abstracts served by the site are shown for
  reference and remain the rights-holders' property.

If you need material beyond non-commercial research or reference use, obtain
it from the original source under that source's terms rather than from here.

## Accuracy

The data is produced by an automated pipeline and is not manually reviewed.
Classification, author identity, affiliation resolution and citation counts
are all incomplete or approximate to a degree documented on the site's About
page and in `public/download/README.md`. It is offered as-is, with no
warranty of accuracy or fitness for any purpose.

## Corrections and removal

If you are an author and your information is shown inaccurately, or you want
your name, affiliation or photo corrected or removed, use the "Report an
error on this page" button in the site's navigation bar. No account is
needed, and the same route covers both a data correction and a privacy
takedown request.
